Preserve the integrity and character of historically
significant neighborhoods when widening roadways and
seeking alternatives.  Consider reducing street width in
appropriate context.
Principle 4.3:  The Cheyenne Area will build a
safe, multimodal transportation system that
consists of streets, sidewalks, bicycle
facilities, and transit.
POLICY 4.3.A:  COMPLETE STREETS
Build arterial and collector streets as complete streets,
providing travel lanes for automobiles and buses, as well
as bicycle facilities and sidewalks.  Ensure safety is a
primary consideration in street design—seek to provide
buffered bicycle lanes when possible and carefully
evaluate the safety of street design on higher-speed
roadways.  Provide for MPO review of all applicable
projects to ensure complete streets integration.
POLICY 4.3.B:  NEIGHBORHOOD DESIGN TO SUPPORT WALKING
