### Page 109 of 188

```text
SHAPE: The Land Use Plan
  COMMUNITY PLAN - 107  
URBAN SERVICES AREA
The Future Land Use Plan establishes an
Urban Service Boundary to distinguish
between the urban and rural portions of the Planning
Area.  Within the Urban Services Boundary, urban-level
development exists or is expected to develop in the
future, meaning development that is connected to
central water and sewer services, and features other
urban amenities such as parks, trails, and protected open
space.  Outside of the Urban Services Boundary, existing
development is limited and future development is not
encouraged in order to retain the rural character, protect
agricultural uses, and maximize investments in services
and infrastructure in the urban area.
```

